  "notes": "Limoneira Company (NASDAQ: LMNR). California-based agribusiness with three reportable segments: Agribusiness (lemons, oranges, avocados, specialty citrus and other crops), Rental Operations (residential / commercial rentals), and Real Estate Development (Harvest at Limoneira / East Area I JV in Santa Paula CA, plus Lewis JV with Lewis Group). Fiscal year ends October 31. Data sourced from SEC EDGAR (CIK 0001342423) 10-K and 10-Q filings plus IR releases. ~10,500 acres of agricultural land owned plus mineral rights and water rights (substantial value not on book). Net debt = total debt (AgWest Farm Credit term + revolver, plus other notes) less cash. EBITDA = company-reported Adjusted EBITDA from earnings releases when available, else operating income + D&A. Lemons report follows complex grower-revenue / packing-revenue mix (fresh and other lemon sales, brokered lemons, lemon byproduct, third-party fruit through Limoneira's packing house). FY24 / FY25 results materially impacted by lemon-pricing weakness and orange-volume cycles, plus the Harvest at Limoneira lot-sale cadence which is lumpy. Pre-FY19 history: Limoneira IPO'd on NASDAQ March 24, 2010 at $14/sh after decades as a private company (founded 1893). Pre-2014 segment reporting was simpler (Agribusiness vs Real Estate / Rental). FY10-FY18 backfill from 10-K Selected Financial Data tables (audited).",
